{"base_label":"Opus 5.5 medium extraction","changes":[{"sheet":"Deal ledger","uid":"c557960e982d47c1cf6822bc","record_label":"Event #62 · by 01/04/2021 · Company I · Did not submit","field":"Flag","before":"","after":"Q10","type":"update"},{"sheet":"Questions","uid":"ed2efa71571247d49d50dace2b7ee011","record_label":"Question Q10","field":null,"before":null,"after":{"Q":"Q10","Question":"Which exit label should represent Company I's disappearance by January 4 when the filing does not report a new missed deadline, withdrawal or exclusion?","Recommended answer":"Keep the supported by-January 4 closure and Not stated reason. Prefer inferred Dropped by target if Alex applies E14's complete-continuing-set convention; retain current Did not submit provisionally until that coding choice is settled.","Why, with page":"Company I bid December 8 and reaffirmed December 29; December 30 directs continued engagement. January 4 names only E and H alongside CLP as still interested (pp. 34-36). No new submission deadline or exit actor is disclosed.","Rows affected":"#62","What changes if answered differently":"Exit label/interpretation changes; the by-January 4 participation bound and bidder counts do not.","Reviewer note":""},"type":"insert"},{"sheet":"Questions","uid":"556c32b5f8f0daa917275083","record_label":"Question Q5","field":"Recommended answer","before":"No: record H only through Other material event rows. No NDA or bid is reported, and being courted is contact, not admission.","after":"Provisionally keep H outside the entered bidder population: the filing records continued solicitation rather than clear diligence-stage admission. Ask Alex whether the December 30 named invitation to seek LOIs is sufficient for admission under E3.","type":"update"},{"sheet":"Questions","uid":"556c32b5f8f0daa917275083","record_label":"Question Q5","field":"What changes if answered differently","before":"If H entered on 12/30, round 3 had one more live strategic bidder, and H needs an exit, Did not submit (inferred) by 01/06/2021.","after":"If H entered December 30, round 3 has one more live strategic bidder and needs an inferred closure at the January 6 selection. Preserve the reported H contacts and type either way.","type":"update"},{"sheet":"Questions","uid":"591493788d9f19fb363aef91","record_label":"Question Q1","field":"Recommended answer","before":"Keep. Alternatives: merge processes 1 and 2 if the Company B merger-of-equals talks (Oct 2018–Mar 2019) count as sale contacts; open R3 at the 12/18–12/21/2020 outreach or the 12/30/2020 selection; treat the 09/17/2020 best-offer request to E as a new round.","after":"Keep the current map provisionally. If Company B's target-proposed merger of equals counts as a sale, process 2 may begin in October 2018; do not automatically merge it with process 1, since the June-to-October gap and undated Liontree outreach need separate treatment. Retain the stated alternative round boundaries.","type":"update"},{"sheet":"Questions","uid":"591493788d9f19fb363aef91","record_label":"Question Q1","field":"What changes if answered differently","before":"Merging P1/P2 deletes #9 and renumbers process 2 rows; a later R3 start moves #48, #49, #50, #51, #52 into R2; a best-offer round would move #37, #38, #39, #40 into a new R2 and make #37 Formal.","after":"Including Company B may move the start of process 2 to October 2018; a merger of processes 1 and 2 requires a separate continuity judgment, not merely inclusion of B. A later R3 start moves #48, #49, #50, #51, #52 into R2; a best-offer round would move #37, #38, #39, #40 into a new R2 and make #37 Formal.","type":"update"},{"sheet":"Deal facts","uid":"f29caaa8f5766a1b55e39a79","record_label":"Deal fact Number of processes","field":"Value","before":"3 (2018; 2019; July 2020–February 2021)","after":"3","type":"update"},{"sheet":"row_review","uid":"141bb813c0b4b84182d7170a","record_label":"Event #49 · 10/27/2020 · Company H · Other material event","field":null,"before":null,"